narrator: Anna is, for the first time, two minutes late.
narrator: She also isn't carrying the notebook.
join anna (Neutral) center
anna: "I wrote a letter. I'm not going to send it."
player: "What kind of letter?"
narrator: She passes you her phone without a word.
narrator: It's a resignation letter to her boss. It is extremely professional. The formal language cannot entirely conceal that the emotional subtext is: please tell me exactly what to do, in detail, always, or I am leaving.
[photo_opportunity id="anna_resignation" patient="anna" title="The Resignation Letter" description="A resignation letter that is structurally a very formal request for micromanagement." portrait="res://assets/photos/anna/resignation_letter.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	narrator: Her expression as she watches you read — anxious, a little mortified, possibly relieved — lands.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 3)
anna: "I'm not going to send it."
player: "You said."
anna: "I just — I needed to write it. To see what it looked like written down."
[stat_check stat="knowledge" base_chance=50 chance_per_point=10]
if {check_result}:
	do GameState.add_stat_xp("knowledge", 1)
	player: "Writing the unsendable letter is a legitimate processing technique. You didn't avoid the feeling — you contained it."
	anna: "That's — yes. That's exactly how it felt."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 8)
else:
	player: "That took some courage to write."
	anna: "I don't know if I'd call it courage."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 3)
- What would happen if you did send it? | [if {patients.anna.trust} >= 50] [else="disable" alt_text="need 50 trust"]
	narrator: She's quiet for a long time.
	anna: "He'd probably accommodate me. He's not a bad manager. He just assumes I prefer autonomy."
	narrator: A pause.
	anna: "Everyone assumes I prefer autonomy."
	player: "Do you?"
	narrator: A longer pause.
	anna: "I prefer things to be correct. And correct requires someone defining correct."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 10)
- What do you want to do about it?
	anna: "I don't know. That's why I'm here."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 2)
if {patients.anna.trust} >= 70 and {flags.anna_named_fixation_s2}:
	anna: "I've been looking into things."
	narrator: She pulls at a thread on her sleeve.
	anna: "There are structured work environments. Very prescriptive project frameworks — mandatory sign-offs, weighted criteria at every stage."
	player: "There are."
	anna: "I've been researching those."
	narrator: A beat.
	anna: "And also other things."
	narrator: She says it in a tone that suggests she has been googling extensively and is now very carefully filing that information into a color-coded internal folder.
	player: "That sounds like progress, Anna."
	anna: "It sounds like homework. I prefer homework to uncertainty."
	player: "I'll write you a rubric."
	narrator: She laughs. It's genuine. First one.
	set {patients.anna.ending} = "breakthrough"
	[add_note patient="anna" note="Breakthrough. Named the preference, began researching practical outlets. Prognosis: good, given sufficient structure."]
else:
	if {patients.anna.trust} < 30:
		narrator: She stands before the session ends. Smooths her jacket precisely.
		anna: "I don't think talking helps. I have a system. The system works."
		narrator: She picks up her bag.
		anna: "Thank you for your time."
		narrator: The door closes. Quietly. Correctly.
		leave anna
		set {patients.anna.ending} = "bad"
		[add_note patient="anna" note="Withdrew before arc completion. Rejected the therapeutic framework. Left with her original premise intact."]
	else:
		anna: "Anyway. The sleep is better."
		player: "Good."
		anna: "And I didn't reorganize your desk today."
		player: "I noticed."
		anna: "Progress."
		narrator: It almost sounds like a question.
		player: "Progress."
		narrator: It almost sounds like an answer.
		set {patients.anna.ending} = "stuck"
		[add_note patient="anna" note="Inconclusive arc. Core fixation unaddressed but coping improved. Left door open for return."]
leave anna
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("anna")
jump between_patients/
